				<wikidot:authorName>Kingreaper</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>60748</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I do really like this tale. Although, I've got to wonder, how does he intend to stabilise when he finally finds a safe reality?</p> <p>I have this image of him finding a reality with the foundation, talking to them, begging them to stabilise him, only to hear &quot;SCP-XXX? That's just a painting that moves! We have no idea how to do what you're asking us.&quot;<br /> And then watching them shift away as he finds himself in a world where the Sasquatch still rule.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-215976#post-1532227</guid>
				<title>Re: Outstanding</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-215976/of-multiverses-and-dandelion-wine#post-1532227</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 09 Aug 2012 11:42:22 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Kingreaper</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>60748</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>That only disproves a large multiverse where one event can instantly destroy the whole thing.</p> <p>A small multiverse where one event could destroy the whole is still possible; as is a multiverse where destruction can only spread slowly between them (as the foundations reality seems to be)</p> <p>Oh, and in Doctor Who, the multiverse is actually relatively small by all signs. There was only one time war, which reached over every reality: The time war didn't happen differently in different realities; and the same is true in terms of the universe bomb, there was only ever one.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-215976#post-1532203</guid>
				<title>Outstanding</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-215976/of-multiverses-and-dandelion-wine#post-1532203</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 09 Aug 2012 10:59:25 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>MrBreaksIt</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1379550</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>One of the better tales I have read, most certainly. You, sir, are a credit to all of us.</p> <p>Also, because I have no idea where else to put this, my disproving of the multiverse: The Multiverse theory states a different reality for every possible situation. There is a Doctor Who episode in which the Daleks build a bomb that would destroy all universes if detonated. This means that there would be a universe out there where the Daleks succeeded. Therefore, if there really were multiple universes, we wouldn't exist. This also proves that the universe is not, in fact, infinite, just very, very large.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
